BACKGROUND/Narrative Baseline for the Way of the Sorcerer: Aberrant Mind : THE IMAGINARY FRIEND (AMBIGUOUS – FLAVOR)
========================================

Since puppyhood, Fenrir has perceived a strange, platypus-like entity.
A watcher. A commentator. A spectator.

Only Fenrir sees it.
It never interferes.
It might be real.
It might be a coping mechanism.

Either way, it is always watching.

========================================
BACKGROUND/Narrative Baseline for the Way of the Peace Domain Clerik
========================================
Unknown to both Fenrir and his gnome owner, the pendant on his collar—given as a simple protection talisman—was consecrated to Gaerdal Ironhand. 
Neither realizes that this small charm places Fenrir, in a subtle and unseen way, under the god’s quiet watch.
Remarkably, Fenrir’s natural mindset—loyal, vigilant, and protective of Pac—mirrors the ideals of Gaerdal Ironhand, planting a seed for a future calling as a Peace Domain cleric.


========================================
BACKGROUND/Narrative Baseline for the Way of the Druid:
========================================
Fenrir was a welcomed—and well-known—guest during the druidic rituals of his gnome owner. 
In a circle where nature, magic, and secrets intertwined, nobody could keep anything hidden from a dog. 
Fenrir quietly observed, learning more than anyone realized.
Whether he remembers the details of those rituals—or can put that knowledge to use in the future—remains to be seen.
